# Conventions

- Read `docs/SPEC.md` (amendments at the top win) and `docs/DECISIONS.md` before changing architecture. Record new decisions there as context → decision → consequence.
- Next.js 16 App Router only, classic ISR (no Cache Components, see D1b). Before using a Next API, read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`. Never use deprecated APIs (`middleware.ts`, single-arg `revalidateTag`, `unstable_cache`).
- TypeScript only, `strict` + `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`. No `any`, no `@ts-ignore`, no disabled lint rule without a justifying comment.
- Server Components by default; `'use client'` only on interactive leaves. Modules imported by Server Components must not import client hooks (split constants into hook-free modules).
- Named exports, except where Next.js requires a default. kebab-case filenames. No barrel files except `src/lib/content/index.ts`. Tests colocated as `*.test.ts(x)`; e2e in `tests/e2e`.
- Environment variables are read only through `src/env.ts` (server-only). The proxy is the one exception and may read `process.env.NODE_ENV`.
- Styling: Tailwind v4 tokens from `src/styles/globals.css` (`@theme`). Default palette is disabled; use tokens (`bg-bg-0`, `text-text-2`, `border-line`…). `cn()` from `@/lib/cn`, variants with `cva`. Dark only: never add `dark:` variants, light themes or `prefers-color-scheme` branches.
- Internal links on public pages use `Link` from `@/i18n/navigation`, never `next/link`.
- Animate only `transform`/`opacity` (and `filter` sparingly). No React state updates per animation frame: write styles through refs in rAF. Every animation respects `useReducedMotionPreference()` / `data-motion='reduced'`.
- Prettier: single quotes, trailing commas, 80 columns, semicolons, LF.
- Conventional Commits, small focused commits, at least one per phase.
